            <member value='&quot;Costa Rica&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Ecuador&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;El Salvador&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Guatemala&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Honduras&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Nicaragua&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Panamá&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Paraguay&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Perú&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;República Dominicana&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Uruguay&quot;' />
            <member value='&quot;Venezuela&quot;' />
          </members>
        </column>
      </datasource-dependencies>
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='6' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='98934' id='5' is-centered='0' param='Image/Encabezado Bajo.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='98770' x='615' y='533'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='4533' id='7' type-v2='text' w='29385' x='25769' y='1667'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='36'>Glossary</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='15133' id='8' is-centered='0' is-scaled='1' param='Image/Size Classification eng.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='32538' x='45231' y='8933' />
        <zone h='9467' id='9' type-v2='text' w='37923' x='2231' y='8400'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontsize='10'>The Whitelist&apos;s purpose is to discriminate good partners from bad partners based on their Vendor Fail Rate (VFR) and Vendor Late (VL) KPI&apos;s. Based on this discriminiation, if a partner is qualified as &apos;apt&apos;, they are able to participate in a marketing campaign without further approval and can be added to the campaign channel in bulk.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>A.  The criteria and processes used to select the partners are as follows:</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='44733' id='10' type-v2='text' w='38692' x='3615' y='17467'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>1.  </run>
            <run fontsize='10'>Only partners from the verticals </run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Restaurant </run>
            <run fontsize='10'>and </run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Coffee </run>
            <run fontsize='10'>and from the </run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Long Tail</run>
            <run fontsize='10'> will be taken into account (Key Accounts are excluded for their preferential treatment). The period of analysis is 28 days (or 4 complete weeks).</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>2. </run>
            <run fontsize='10'> Partners are classified, depending on their order volume (only confirmed orders), into 4 categories:</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>        -  Big</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>        -  Medium</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>        -  Small</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>        -  Too Small</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Big</run>
            <run fontsize='10'> partners belong to th 90th percentile, meaning they are part of the 10% with the most confirmed orders. </run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Medium</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>&apos;s are between the 60th and the 90th and </run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Small </run>
            <run fontsize='10'>partners are below the 60th percentil. Partners with less than 25 confirmed orders throughout the period are considered </run>
            <run fontsize='10' italic='true'>Too Small</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>. See figure on the right.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>3.</run>
            <run fontsize='10'>  Each of these size groups will be assigned a maximum value for their VFR and VL, with the objective of classifying as &apos;apt&apos; around 60% of partners (as shwon in the table to the right). With the purpose of extending the VL limit for those partners that have a very low VFR and viceversa, a line is drawn between these limits in a scatter plot, and those partners below it will be classified as &apos;apt&apos;. Please refer to the scatter plots to the right to see the difference between apt and inapt partners, and how apt partners condense at the bottom left corner.</run>
            <run>

The limits for VFR and VL in each size category are different for each country

</run>
            <run bold='true' fontsize='10'>4.</run>
            <run fontsize='10'><![CDATA[ Marketplace partners, or logistic partners that don't have a VL KPI assigned, will only be classified by their VFR KPI, which has to be smaller than <[Parameters].[Parameter 3]> of the maxVFR for that size category.]]></run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='2400' id='11' type-v2='text' w='40231' x='2000' y='60133'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontsize='10'>B.  Criteria for franchises will be developed for the next iteration of the Whitelist.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='6133' id='24' name='Size Limits' show-title='false' w='17923' x='3615' y='37200' />
        <zone h='2933' id='25' mode='compact' param='[Parameters].[Parameter 1]' type-v2='paramctrl' w='12308' x='20769' y='37867' />
      </zones>
